Rider-Waite-Smith Tarot — copyright status

Original artwork
----------------
Illustrations by Pamela Colman Smith, created under the direction of
Arthur Edward Waite and first published by William Rider & Son in
December 1909.

The original artwork is in the public domain in the United States
(published before 1929) and in jurisdictions applying a life-of-the-
author term of 70 years or less (Pamela Colman Smith died in 1951;
copyright expired in the United Kingdom and the EU at the end of 2021).

Digital restoration
-------------------
The scanned and cleaned images in this directory were obtained from an
anonymous restoration published on Anna's Archive and offered under
CC0 1.0 Universal.

Under United States law, a faithful photographic reproduction of a
two-dimensional public domain work does not attract a new copyright
(Bridgeman Art Library v. Corel Corp., 36 F. Supp. 2d 191 (S.D.N.Y.
1999)). Jurisdictions that recognise a separate right in reproductions
may reach a different result; the CC0 dedication is relied upon in that
case.

Trademarks
----------
"Rider-Waite" and related marks are claimed by U.S. Games Systems, Inc.
Trademark rights are distinct from copyright and are not affected by
the public domain status of the artwork. This deck is not affiliated
with or endorsed by U.S. Games Systems, Inc.

Packaging
